{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-atomic-lp-stability","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:atomic-lp-stability","kind":"proposition","title":"LP stability of the atomic braid","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-atomic-braid"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability","text":"atomic-lp-stability.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:atomic-lp-stability\"></a><p><em>The bare hydrogen atom <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[e, \\mathfrak{p}] = \\sigma_0^{-1}</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_2(q)</code> is <strong>LP-unstable</strong>: there exists a Markov-normalised operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X^* = \\alpha \\cdot \\mathbf{1} + \\beta \\cdot \\sigma_0</code> that annihilates the traced volume (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V = 0</code>).</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/atomic-lp-stability.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"14.8.1","page":"b/prop-atomic-lp-stability","qa":{"counts":{"pass":64,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":54,"unknown":0,"stale":110},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.atomic_lp_stability","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Confinement/atomic_lp_stability.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
